# Plan storage and archiving

## Where plans live

All plans that have not been built yet live together in `~/.cursor/plans/`. When a new plan is written (Plan mode or a plan doc), save it there rather than in this repo (`.cursor/plans/`, `docs/`, `sitehub_worker_Ready/docs/`). If an unbuilt plan turns up elsewhere, move it into `~/.cursor/plans/` and update any links to it.

## Archive executed plans

When a plan has been fully executed (all its todos done and the user has confirmed or the work is complete), move it as the final step of the task:

| Plan location | Archive to |
|---|---|
| `~/.cursor/plans/` | `~/.cursor/plans/old plans/` |
| Older plan docs still in this repo (e.g. `*_PLAN.md` under `docs/`) | `docs/old plans/` |

- Use `git mv` for files tracked by git, plain `mv` otherwise. Keep the original filename.
- Only archive plans that were actually executed; leave partially done or not-started plans in place.
- Never archive these active plans unless the user says so:
  - `~/.cursor/plans/OFFLINE_SIGN_IN_PLAN.md` (Stage 0 of the Site Access and Permits Roadmap; archive both together once that roadmap is fully executed)
  - `~/.cursor/plans/investor_differentiation_roadmap_f3e86d8d.plan.md`
- Mention the move in the final summary to the user.
